It turns out no matter how powerful a character is at the
start, the monsters in the game can always end up more
powerful.

I die a lot by rushing into situations too dangerous for my
character.  With a weak starting character that can happen
in the first couple of steps into the mines.  With a strong
character that can happen deep in the mines.  Build a very
powerful class and it just happens deeper than that.

It's the same as the joke about the RNG granting an early
wish and then killing you later - The most common with is
for blessed +3 gray/silver dragon scale mail.  The most
common result is aggressively rushing deeper until the
added AC points no longer help.

I found this to be the single hardest lesson to learn in the
early game.  To this day I still lose most of my characters
to it and my percentage only grows very gradually.

The reason the lesson is so hard to learn is it's strategic
not tactical.  As you have just done there's a huge
temptation to think your character died for tactical reasons
and if you handle that exact situation better in the future
you'll make it deeper.  The probelm with the tactical
approach is eventually you get so deeply in trouble no
amount of tactics will ever help.  That's what happens when
save scumming as well.

Seriously - The way to learn this lesson is to play weaker
starts not stronger starts.  Then use the experience to learn
caution and strategy not aggression and tactics.


